// All i learn in day 1 (Semantic HTML)
Semantic HTML is using a tag HTML that describing the content inside and the function of the element, not only for the looks.
this also help Search Engine Optimization to read your website.

1. 
<header>
    <h1>For example</h1>
</header>

for header or opening in website like logo, navigation, website title, and many more.

2.
<nav>
    <a href="#">Home</a>
    <a href="#">Article</a>
    <a href="#">Contact</a>
</nav>

for navigation link menu in website.

3. 
<main>
    <h2>New Article</h2>
</main>

for the main content of the website. Only 1 main in 1 page.

4. 
<section>
    <p>bla bla bla ...</p>
</section>

for a content with different theme. for example products and testimonials.

5.
<article>
    <h1>News</h1>
    <p>...</p>
</article>

for content like article, news, review, forum, and many more.

6.
<aside>
    more article
</aside>

for content that not the main content. like ads, sidebar, and more.

7. 
<footer>
    &copy writer 2026 - indonesia
</footer>

for the end content of the website. used to fill with social media, copyright, contact, and many more.




